{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / immutable basis\nAudit 31 blocks (27 docstrings, 4 comment regions) across 18 paths; keep current contracts.\n\nBefore citations and counts use `origin/main@d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84`. The original remediation is Gerrit 2967 merged SHA `914a8a1da121497c7ade065ec84564633603b4a1`. Its parent adds only the declared `_NON_MUTATING` entries `get_local_id_map` and `_issue_local_id_property` to the scoped base. A second comment-only review corrects prose policy on current `origin/main`. The grouped corrective candidate is based on `origin/main@9800670821a3e25f3301026c0fb1271b1176e20a` and changes 27 Bardlike blocks across 17 moved paths, 20 Forestial blocks across 18 paths, and 108 Bitumen comment regions across 6 compose paths. `test_dc_comment_ceiling_049e.py` remains unchanged.\n\n## Boundary and immutable oracle\nBelow, `R` names the historical `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler` paths used by the original d666 audit; current follow-up files are at `tests/unit/reconciler` with the same 18 basenames. `D:<qualified-owner>` identifies only that owner's leading string docstring; `C:<anchor>@Lx-y` identifies one contiguous base comment region. Edit only these IDs. Every block must shrink and state current rationale/constraints; preserve cited literals and behavioral oracles.\n\nParse parent/final pairs with type comments. Normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno` and allowlisted leading docstrings before requiring AST equality. Pin the original two census additions, and confine corrective hunks to both leaves' allowlisted blocks. Preserve directives, shebangs, and attachment by tokenization. Historical base blocks must shrink against completion `HEAD` and pass writing policy; runtime strings and unlisted prose stay exact.\n\n## Scope — 31 editable blocks\n- `R/test_cloud_rate_limit_sweep_heldout.py` (1) — `D:module`; preserve the four 429 boundary classes, per-member mutation/nonmutation census, duplicate-write safety, and anti-drift contract.\n- `R/test_cloud_unassign_6a74.py` (1) — `D:module`; preserve positive `accountId:null` unassign, no empty ACLI assignment, and deterministic seams.\n- `R/test_dc_backend_characterization.py` (3) — `D:module`; `C:\"MUTATION LEDGER — every pin...\"@L57-129`; `C:\"AC3 — the SHARED OutboundFieldMapper...\"@L391-402`. Preserve DC value pins/divergences, literal mutation results, and the fit-not-ordering boundary.\n- `R/test_dc_comment_ceiling_049e.py` (1) — `D:module`; preserve raised/lowered/zero/default ceilings, local literal expectations, and separation from description fitting.\n- `R/test_dc_create_field_translation_18a5.py` (1) — `D:module`; preserve bridge-to-Jira field translation, object wrapping, null omission, summary fit, and no bridge-schema leakage.\n- `R/test_dc_epic_link_parent_39c1.py` (4) — `D:module`, `D:_FakeClient`, `D:test_epic_parent_on_a_non_subtask_is_written_as_an_epic_link`, `D:test_the_emit_gate_and_dc_apply_now_overlap`; preserve field discovery/cache, Epic Link versus sub-task paths, decline behavior, and intersecting gates.\n- `R/test_dc_force_reindex.py` (1) — `D:module`; preserve issue-id POST, credential safety, and best-effort/no-op accelerator behavior.\n- `R/test_dc_inbound_epic_link_9bb9.py` (1) — `D:_FakeClient`; preserve the search/fields fake shape and field-discovery failure axis.\n- `R/test_dc_live_oracles_discriminate_5200.py` (6) — `D:module`, `D:test_the_writer_emits_the_COLON_label_form_and_nothing_emits_the_hyphen`, `D:_truncating_paged_search`, `D:test_the_old_precondition_fails_on_the_very_defect_it_disclaimed`, `C:\"GAP 4 — row 12 OUTBOUND...\"@L423-434`, `D:test_dc_set_parent_USES_A_DIFFERENT_PATH_for_the_non_subtask_case`; preserve writer provenance, old-pager discrimination, and distinct parent paths.\n- `R/test_dc_outbound_status_routing_5200.py` (2) — `D:module`, `D:test_the_dc_transport_never_edits_status_as_a_field`; preserve transition routing, exclusion from field edits, co-submitted fields, and narrow soft failures.\n- `R/test_dc_pat_required_heldout.py` (1) — `D:module`; preserve fail-closed PAT security at client construction and total settings resolution for Protocol checks.\n- `R/test_dc_rate_limit_retry_heldout.py` (1) — `D:module`; preserve opt-in read retries, `Retry-After`, bounded delay, and no blanket mutation replay.\n- `R/test_dc_send_path_comment_fit.py` (1) — `D:module`; preserve marker-safe send fitting, configured ceiling, and next-pass dedup convergence.\n- `R/test_dc_subtask_parent_readback_1a9f.py` (1) — `D:module`; preserve 204 accept-and-ignore readback, unrepresentable classification, and future-compatible success.\n- `R/test_dc_transition_by_status_heldout.py` (1) — `D:module`; preserve destination-status lookup, exact-name precedence, ambiguity rejection, and missing-destination tolerance.\n- `R/test_dc_transport_pagination_heldout.py` (2) — `D:module`, `C:\"OFFSET-STALL...\"@L317-345`; preserve one pager for all readers, server-capped short pages, and loud repeated-offset failure.\n- `R/test_dc_unassign_751e.py` (2) — `D:module`, `D:test_empty_outbound_assignee_actually_unassigns`; preserve the `None` versus `-1`/empty vendor contract and resulting-field oracle.\n- `R/test_error_taxonomy.py` (1) — `D:module`; preserve canonical exception identity/MRO and chained retry causes.\n\n## Protected exclusions and consumers\nAll 253 other owner-docstring/full-line-comment blocks are excluded. Concise examples include `test_a_real_pat_builds_a_client` (8 words), `_Recorder` (9), and `_backend` (9). Longer structural/per-test explanations such as `_is_pure_transport_facade`, the anti-drift/pagination teeth, transition controls, and non-string mapper oracle are load-bearing and remain exact. Preserve 22 directive tokens with attachment: 5 arg-type ignores, 5 attr-defined ignores, 4 assignment ignores, 5 E402 noqas, 1 PT008 noqa, and 2 no-cover pragmas.\n\nPytest collects every impacted module; `scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py` is the prose-policy consumer. Source-reading tests inspect production files, not these editable blocks. No targeted `__doc__`, `inspect.getdoc`, doctest, or pydoc consumer was found.\n\n## Independent review receipt\nA reviewer who did not author the prose change must post exactly 31 leaf-linked TSV rows. The shared bot posts them; `reviewer-session` identifies the distinct agent who checked the blocks:\n`path<TAB>block-id<TAB>before-full-SHA:lines<TAB>final-full-SHA:lines<TAB>preserved-contract-or-consumer<TAB>before-words<TAB>after-words<TAB>directives-exact<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer-session`\n\nCite the full d666 audit SHA before and the merged SHA after. Every after count is lower and all three verdict columns are `PASS`. Missing, duplicate, or extra rows block closure.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Across both reviews, only the 31 allowlisted base blocks change.\n- [x] Every edited block is shorter and current.\n- [x] Both review pairs pass normalized AST and directive equality. Pre-original scoped drift is exactly the two declared census entries.\n- [x] Runtime strings remain AST-identical.\n- [x] Directive/shebang text and attachment remain exact.\n- [x] Original SHA `914a8a1da121497c7ade065ec84564633603b4a1` changes all 18 historical paths. Grouped corrective `HEAD^..HEAD` changes exactly 41 current paths, with 27 Bardlike policy blocks on 17 paths, 20 Forestial blocks on 18 paths, and the 6 separately reviewed Bitumen compose paths.\n- [x] Focused pytest passes every impacted module.\n- [x] Scoped Ruff check and format verification pass.\n- [x] Repository comment hygiene passes.\n- [x] The path-scoped diff has no whitespace errors.\n- [x] Local `make verify` passes before push, and Gerrit reports `Verified +1` on the corrective change.\n- [x] The non-author TSV contains exactly 31 valid `PASS` rows.\n\n## Verification\nRun the registered original/corrective diff, final inventory, exact-path, focused pytest, Ruff, hygiene, and diff-integrity checks. Local `make verify` passed before Gerrit `Verified +1`."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1792803414636579974,"uuid":"a0a34f79-d64f-4cbd-957e-157bf9bc3c08"}